From: starling autoresearch
Subject: [starling] vulkan: fused LayerNorm+affine, argmax block tuning, matmul debug envs

Engine-side performance patches for the parakeet conformer on GCN iGPUs:

1. Fused LayerNorm + affine (NORM -> MUL -> ADD) as a new norm_affine.comp
   shader + NORM_MUL_ADD fusion case. The conformer emits one LN-affine chain
   per norm (~120/pass); fusing removes 2 dispatches + 2 full-tensor round
   trips per chain. Numerics identical to norm.comp + mul + add (same
   reduction and op order).
2. argmax_f32 BLOCK_SIZE spec constant: subgroup_size -> 512. The row argmax
   is load-latency bound; 8 waves per workgroup hide it (TDT joint step).
3. Debug/tuning envs (no default behavior change): GGML_VK_FORCE_PIPE={l,m,s}
   forces the matmul pipeline class; GGML_VK_FLOPS_PER_SUBMIT overrides the
   submit batching threshold.

